        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eve Beglarian, Zach Bogosian, Jack Roslovic, Evander Kane, Tyler Myers, Drew Stafford, Joel Armia, Brendan Lemieux\n- Products: Overstepping\n- Organizations: Winnipeg Jets, Buffalo Sabres\n- Places: Ann Arbor, Michigan, United States\n- Roles: composer, performer, audio producer, ice hockey player\n\nFacts:\n- Eve Beglarian was born in Ann Arbor, Michigan, United States, on July 22, 1958.\n- Eve Beglarian is a contemporary American composer, performer, and audio producer of Armenian descent.\n- Overstepping is the 1998 debut album by avant-garde composer Eve Beglarian.\n- Zachary M. Bogosian is also identified as Zach Bogosian, and his name is given in Armenian as \u0017\u001d\u000e\u0017\u001b\r\n \u0014.\n- The Winnipeg Jets acquired a draft pick in a trade that sent Evander Kane and Zach Bogosian to the Buffalo Sabres.\n- In that trade, the Buffalo Sabres sent Tyler Myers, Drew Stafford, Joel Armia, and Brendan Lemieux to the Winnipeg Jets.",
